E1c-control — UNIFORM coarse, the honest comparator for graded.

E1c coarsens the air from a FINE base (sf 1.0). The question is not "does that
work" but "does it beat simply using a coarse uniform mesh of the same size".
Without this control, a graded result proves only that fewer elements are
cheaper, which was never in doubt.

Same transparent-dielectric test bed — full loaded geometry, every eps = 1.0, so
physics.spectrum() is still exact — at UNIFORM size factors that are known to
mesh (2.0 and 1.5; 2.5 and 1.2 both fail, non-monotonically).

VERIFICATION   physics.spectrum(), exact.
FALSIFICATION  if uniform sf 2.0 matches graded k=3 on accuracy at similar
               element count, GRADING BUYS NOTHING and the extra knob should be
               removed rather than kept.

